# Page pattern (`app/**/page.tsx`)

Pages are **thin server entry points**. No UI markup, no forms, no `ShadowBox` / `SectionHeader` — that belongs in `src/views/`.

## Responsibilities (page only)

1. `generateMetadata` — i18n title/description from `params.locale`
2. Resolve `locale` from `params` with `isValidLocale` + `i18nConfig.defaultLocale`
3. Compose layout + view and pass `locale` down

## Standard shape

```typescript
import type { Metadata } from 'next';
import getTranslations from '@/i18n';
import { LoginView } from '@views/auth/LoginView';
import { WithMainLayout } from '@hocs/WithMainLayout';
import { isValidLocale } from '@shared/config/locales/locale';
import type { Language } from '@shared/config/locales/types';
import i18nConfig from '@/i18nConfig';

type LoginPageProps = {
    params: Promise<{ locale: string }>;
};

const i18nNamespaces = ['common'];

export async function generateMetadata({
    params,
}: LoginPageProps): Promise<Metadata> {
    const { locale } = await params;
    const { t } = await getTranslations(locale, i18nNamespaces);

    return {
        title: t('common:page.login.title'),
        description: t('common:page.login.description'),
    };
}

export default async function LoginPage({ params }: LoginPageProps) {
    const { locale: localeParam } = await params;
    const locale: Language = isValidLocale(localeParam)
        ? localeParam
        : i18nConfig.defaultLocale;
    const Layouted = WithMainLayout(LoginView);

    return <Layouted locale={locale} />;
}
```

Reference: [`app/[locale]/(Auth)/login/page.tsx`](app/[locale]/(Auth)/login/page.tsx), [`app/[locale]/(Auth)/verify-email/page.tsx`](app/[locale]/(Auth)/verify-email/page.tsx).

## View owns UI

- `ShadowBox`, `SectionHeader`, `Legend`, action buttons
- `<Suspense>` around client children that use `useSearchParams()`
- Client forms and verification flows

Reference: [`src/views/auth/LoginView.tsx`](src/views/auth/LoginView.tsx), [`src/views/auth/VerifyEmailView.tsx`](src/views/auth/VerifyEmailView.tsx).

## Layout placement

| Pattern | Where | When |
|---------|-------|------|
| `WithMainLayout(View)` in **page** | `const Layouted = WithMainLayout(MyView); return <Layouted locale={locale} />` | Auth and most marketing pages |
| `WithMainLayout` inside **view** | View calls `WithMainLayout` and returns `<Layouted />` | Feature views that bundle layout + content (e.g. create group) |

Prefer **layout in page** for new routes unless the view already wraps itself.

## Do not put in `page.tsx`

- `ShadowBox`, `SectionHeader`, form components
- `getTranslations` for view copy (only for `generateMetadata` unless the page has no view)
- `getCurrentLangFromPathname()` — use `params.locale` (see `.cursor/rules/locale-pattern.mdc`)
- Business logic, fetch, or API calls — use the view, tRPC caller, or server modules

## Protected / no-index pages

Add `robots: { index: false, follow: false }` in `generateMetadata` when needed (e.g. `/app`, `/create`).

## Checklist for a new page

- [ ] `PageProps` with `params: Promise<{ locale: string }>`
- [ ] `i18nNamespaces` constant
- [ ] `generateMetadata` uses `getTranslations(locale, i18nNamespaces)`
- [ ] Default export resolves `locale` and renders `<Layouted locale={locale} />` or `<MyView locale={locale} />`
- [ ] No inline UI — delegate to `src/views/...`
